$DIR/test.p:88:60: tag field u of packed union P must come before the first variant
    A packed union has a backing type, which fixes its size, and exactly one
    named field before its variants: the tag. The tag is a bool, integer or enum
    field that occupies the same bits in every variant, and each variant lists
    the tag values that select it.
    (see "Unions" in the Plutonium spec, section 7.13)
    (run "pluto explain E2407" for a longer explanation)
